// RZI - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

# RZI is the run-length encoding images use: a count of two or more
# followed by the value, and singletons emitted literally. Runs over
# the bytes of "Hello World!":
#   1 x 'H'
#   1 x 'e'
#   2 x 'l'
#   1 x 'o'
#   1 x ' '
#   1 x 'W'
#   1 x 'o'
#   1 x 'r'
#   1 x 'l'
#   1 x 'd'
#   1 x '!'
